   "tag": "h1",
   "text": "Is Quantum Healing Hypnosis Technique (QHHT) Safe?",
   "section": "comp-m04zcdxw"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Updated: Jan 5",
   "section": "comp-m04zcdxw"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "The answer is YES. QHHT is considered a safe, gentle, and deeply relaxing process when facilitated by a trained practitioner. You remain aware, in control, and able to speak or stop at any time.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "What QHHT Really Is",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "I have occasionally seen the word hypnotherapy misinterpreted or even mistakenly linked to the idea of therapy as (rape), which is false. Hypnotherapy also known as Hypnosis or Hypnos comes from the Greek word which translates to be asleep, even though a person under hypnosis is not actually asleep.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "What QHHT does is to guide you into a calm, focused state in which your mind can access memories, insights, and inner wisdom more easily. When many people think of hypnosis, they think of mind control, but in reality, under QHHT you cannot be compelled to do anything against your will.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Who QHHT Can Help",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "QHHT is a calm, empowering experience designed to support inner healing. With a qualified practitioner, it provides a safe space to gain clarity, reduce stress, build confidence, release old beliefs and patterns which no longer serve and replace them with more positive ones, and connect with a deeper sense of self.",
   "section": ""
  },
